From a53d6f5cd05679ac4e4c747295bbbeed215cb03f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:14:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] board: nvidia: add SHIELD TV 2017 (P2894, darcy)

U-Boot runs as a second stage after NVIDIA's cboot, which starts it as
the kernel of an Android boot image and leaves the board set up.

The board code touches no hardware. It reads cboot's device tree for
the HDMI framebuffer (to drive U-Boot's console through
simple-framebuffer), the boot image's ramdisk (a FIT image to boot) and
the board revision, reports them on screen, and passes the framebuffer
on to the kernel. The environment is never stored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
